WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.844 --> 00:00:04.919
On line 3 too-light cartons keep coming out of the filling unit.

2
00:00:05.992 --> 00:00:08.360
The module Engineering problem solving is

3
00:00:08.407 --> 00:00:11.518
about how plants find root causes and improve.

4
00:00:12.511 --> 00:00:13.765
You are the engineer.

5
00:00:14.468 --> 00:00:17.591
After the shift you and the team lead fix it for good.

6
00:00:18.655 --> 00:00:21.383
First you find the cause and gather the facts.

7
00:00:22.462 --> 00:00:25.515
Then you try out the improvement and make it last.

8
00:00:26.856 --> 00:00:29.422
The first topic is Finding the root cause.

9
00:00:30.137 --> 00:00:32.447
A too-light carton is only the symptom.

10
00:00:33.455 --> 00:00:38.505
The root cause is the cause that, once removed, stops the problem coming back.

11
00:00:39.536 --> 00:00:43.158
You keep asking why until you find a cause you can act on.

12
00:00:44.218 --> 00:00:48.258
If an answer has several causes, you draw a why tree on the board.

13
00:00:49.581 --> 00:00:53.064
The second topic is Facts, data and experiments.

14
00:00:53.766 --> 00:00:56.332
You go and see for yourself where it happens.

15
00:00:57.364 --> 00:01:00.058
A report shows what someone chose to record.

16
00:01:00.813 --> 00:01:04.041
On the floor you count and measure, and test what you think.

17
00:01:05.083 --> 00:01:08.543
You watch from an Ohno circle, a chalk circle on the floor.

18
00:01:09.855 --> 00:01:12.943
The third topic is PDCA and the A3.

19
00:01:13.625 --> 00:01:15.610
An improvement is an experiment.

20
00:01:16.693 --> 00:01:18.678
You predict what a countermeasure does.

21
00:01:19.692 --> 00:01:24.707
You try it out small, in a trial on one machine, and see whether it holds.

22
00:01:25.695 --> 00:01:29.306
The story of the problem fits on one sheet, the A3.

23
00:01:30.565 --> 00:01:33.328
The fourth topic is Kaizen and the value stream.

24
00:01:34.015 --> 00:01:36.546
You improve step by step, with the team.

25
00:01:37.581 --> 00:01:41.575
Small improvements every day, sometimes an event of a few days.

26
00:01:42.596 --> 00:01:46.462
You also draw the value stream, to see where the material waits.

27
00:01:47.498 --> 00:01:51.910
When an operator pulls the cord of the andon, the team lead comes to help.

28
00:01:52.922 --> 00:01:57.206
That is how you tackle line 3, until the problem stops coming back.

29
00:01:58.530 --> 00:01:59.331
The whole map.

30
00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:04.715
The first station is Engineering problem solving, in Making the plant better.

31
00:02:05.755 --> 00:02:07.949
Each of the four topics has four levels.

32
00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:11.594
Start at Basics level with 5 whys.

33
00:02:12.314 --> 00:02:14.810
You learn to tell symptom from root cause.

34
00:02:15.919 --> 00:02:19.158
At Working knowledge level come the limits of 5 whys,

35
00:02:19.298 --> 00:02:22.862
breaking down, the A3 report and value stream mapping.

36
00:02:23.879 --> 00:02:27.699
At Advanced level come is and is not, measuring before concluding,

37
00:02:27.908 --> 00:02:30.346
the 8D and facilitating a session.

38
00:02:31.379 --> 00:02:33.922
At Expert level come verifying the fix,

39
00:02:34.108 --> 00:02:38.044
experiment design, reviewing an A3 and an improvement system.
